# SM3 Studio - what must never be committed
#
# This repository holds OUR code, notes and measurements, and nothing else. Everything that comes
# from Spider-Man 3 (or from Spider-Man: Web of Shadows), every 3D model and texture, every built
# file and every personal setting stays out. The rules are deliberately broad: when in doubt, a
# file is ignored. To publish a file of a blocked type on purpose (a screenshot in docs/, say),
# add an explicit "!" exception below and write down why. See README.md, "What this repository
# does not contain".

# --- Game data, rebuilt on each player's machine ----------------------------------------------
# tools/extraire_donnees_jeu.py writes these folders from the player's own copy of the game.
# They belong to Activision/Treyarch: never commit them.
/vanilla/

# profiles/: everything is ignored except our README and our own measurement files (numbers and
# SHA-256 fingerprints, no game bytes). The pattern "dir/*" + "!dir/" + "dir/*" + "!file" is the
# way git allows re-including a file inside an ignored folder.
/profiles/*
!/profiles/README.md
!/profiles/blacksuit/
/profiles/blacksuit/*
!/profiles/blacksuit/comparison.json
!/profiles/blacksuit/frames.json
!/profiles/venom/
/profiles/venom/*
!/profiles/venom/roundtrip_validation.json
# Spider-Man: Web of Shadows profile (another game; copied by hand from an older installation).
# Only sources.json, the SHA-256 list of the two exports SM3 Studio recognises, is ours.
!/profiles/rvb/
/profiles/rvb/*
!/profiles/rvb/sources.json

# Venom research folders. support_venom_atlas/ used to hold a modified copy of a game pack: only
# its README is published. support_venom_direct/ builds files from the player's Game.exe and mod
# (shaders.h is game bytecode); its own .gitignore lists them too, this is a second safety net.
/support_venom_atlas/*
!/support_venom_atlas/README.md
/support_venom_direct/shaders.h
/support_venom_direct/atlas_signature.*
/support_venom_direct/installation.json
/support_venom_direct/shader_build.json
*.asm
*.lib
*.exp

# --- Game file types, wherever they appear ---------------------------------------------------
# Packs and the loose resources xeSM3 loads (also the 0x<hash>.<name>.wrap.* resources).
*.PCPACK
*.pcpack
*.PCAPK
*.pcapk
*.PAK
*.pak
*.toc
*.apkf
*.mesh
*.skel
*.mat
*.tex
*.anim
*.dds
*.fsb
*.bik
# Raw blobs: texture headers (*.hdr68.bin), shader bytecode, Game.exe.costume_mat_origine.bin,
# venom_direct_material.bin...
*.bin
# Game.exe, its copies and backups (Game.exe.original, Game.exe.sauvegarde_patchs_sm3, ...), and
# every executable or library: SM3 Studio.exe is built from this repository, Windows' winmm.dll
# is copied from the player's own system (support_venom_direct/install.py).
Game.exe*
*.sauvegarde_patchs_sm3
*.exe
*.exe.*
*.dll

# --- 3D models, textures and archives -------------------------------------------------------
# Models and their textures are their authors' work (and often rips of other games). The
# formats are those SM3 Studio accepts as a source (sm3_convertir.FORMATS / IMAGES).
*.glb
*.gltf
*.fbx
*.obj
*.dae
*.ply
*.stl
*.x3d
*.abc
*.usd
*.usda
*.usdc
*.blend
*.blend1
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.tga
*.bmp
*.tif
*.tiff
*.webp
*.psd
*.zip
*.rar
*.7z
# Pictures made for the documentation are allowed, in docs/ only.
!/docs/**/*.png
!/docs/**/*.jpg

# --- Built and generated files --------------------------------------------------------------
# build/<mod>/ = intermediate files of each conversion; mods/<mod>/ = the deliverable mods.
/build/
/mods/
# PyInstaller output (construire/README.md).
/construire/dist/
/construire/work/
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
# Traces written next to meshes (finger and section-split traces) and other numpy dumps.
*.npz
# Half-written files (interrupted extraction, settings replaced atomically).
*.tmp
# Logs: install.log / boucle.log (Install and launch game), venom_direct.log... They hold
# personal paths.
*.log
# Backups that the installers make in the game folder, if one ever lands here.
SM3_Studio_Backups/
mods.config.ini*

# --- Personal settings ----------------------------------------------------------------------
# Written by the window next to SM3 Studio.exe (or next to the sources): blender.exe path,
# project folder, game folder, last model, every field of the window.
/sm3_studio.json
# The interface language chosen at the first start.
/language.txt

# --- Editors and operating system -----------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
.idea/
*.swp
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini
